## 🧠 CLIENTS PAGE PHILOSOPHY

This page answers **one powerful question**:

> “Which clients are good for my business — and which are risky?”

Not contact storage.
Not sales CRM.
**Payment behavior insight.**

---

# 🧱 PAGE LAYOUT (DESKTOP)

```
┌──── Page Header ─────────────────────┐
│ Clients                              │
│ Subtitle: Payment behavior overview │
└──────────────────────────────────────┘

┌──── Clients Table (main) ────────────┐
│ Client rows                          │
└──────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Simple. No filters overload.

---

# 1️⃣ PAGE HEADER

### Title:

**Clients**

### Subtitle:

> “View payment behavior and outstanding balances”

❌ No “Add Client” button
Clients are created automatically when invoices are added.

This removes friction.

---

# 2️⃣ CLIENTS TABLE (CORE)

### Columns (carefully chosen):

1. Client Name
2. Total Outstanding
3. Overdue Amount
4. Avg Payment Delay
5. Open Invoices
6. Risk Indicator
7. Action

---

### Risk Indicator (VERY IMPORTANT)

Use simple signals:

* 🟢 Good (usually pays on time)
* 🟡 Slow (occasional delays)
* 🔴 Risky (frequent late payments)

This is insanely valuable to founders.

---

# 3️⃣ ROW INTERACTION

Clicking a row → **Client Detail Page**

Hover → subtle highlight

No inline editing.

---

# 4️⃣ CLIENT DETAIL PAGE (SECOND LEVEL)

This opens when a client row is clicked.

### Top Section:

* Client Name
* Contact info
* Total outstanding
* Avg delay

---

### Middle:

**Invoices for this client**

* Invoice #
* Amount
* Status
* Due date

Clickable rows → Invoice Detail

---

### Bottom:

**Notes / History**

* “Always delays by 15 days”
* “Prefers WhatsApp follow-ups”

This becomes relationship intelligence.

---

# 5️⃣ VISUAL STYLE

* Table > cards (desktop)
* Risk color used very sparingly
* Numbers slightly bolded
* No charts initially

---

# 6️⃣ EMPTY STATES

### No clients yet

Text:

> “Clients will appear here once you add invoices.”

Simple. Reassuring.

---

